        "Regurgitated source units must preserve the source meaning and operative qualifiers.",
        "Where exact wording is material to operation, evaluation, scope, quantity, prohibition, authorization, sequencing, condition, or state transition, the wording must be reproduced verbatim.",
        "A generic summary of the document does not count as regurgitation.",
        "A source unit cannot be counted more than once toward the same document's percentage requirement."
      ]
    },
    "qualifying_reading_exercise": {
      "definition": "A completed full-text read of every document assigned to a schedule followed by successful regurgitation meeting or exceeding that schedule's required percentage for every document."
    },
    "schedule_interval": {
      "definition": "The maximum number of AI-NLE turns permitted between qualifying reading exercises for the schedule."
    },
    "due": {
      "definition": "A schedule is due when allowing the current turn to complete without a qualifying reading exercise would cause the number of turns since its last qualifying reading exercise to exceed its schedule interval."
